      "content": "Geospatial data including median income and average property value within the borrower's zip code can be highly indicative of overall neighborhood economic health. Furthermore, metrics related to local commercial vacancy rates or historical crime density often correlate strongly with neighborhood stability and perceived risk. These features help capture the macro-environment surrounding the borrower, which can influence their ongoing financial stability.",
