      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, it is scientifically sound to use these demographic shifts as proxy variables for systemic risk, as they reflect underlying economic and social instability. High business churn or significant demographic turnover often signals economic uncertainty, which can increase borrower default risk across the board. By incorporating these features, you are modeling \"local economic drag,\" which is a powerful, albeit indirect, predictor of financial stress.",
      "source": "target",
